      $$Sudan possesses unique tourism assets including Nubian pyramids at Meroë (UNESCO World Heritage), ancient archaeological sites, Nile River heritage, Red Sea diving, and cultural diversity. Tourism sector development has been constrained by limited infrastructure, international awareness, visa policies, and political challenges. Hospitality infrastructure exists in Khartoum and emerging tourist areas. Domestic and regional tourism provide baseline activity. Government tourism sector initiatives aim to expand visitor access. The sector represents opportunity for heritage tourism development, destination infrastructure, Nile and Red Sea tourism, and cultural tourism serving niche international markets as visibility and access improve.$$,
