      $$Tunisia produces modest oil and gas domestically while importing to meet energy demand. The country is expanding renewable energy including solar and wind projects, with government targets for renewable penetration. Energy efficiency programs address consumption patterns. Regional power interconnection with Algeria and Libya supports energy security. Energy sector reforms aim to attract private investment in generation and renewables. Solar and wind potential in southern regions support development. The sector represents opportunity for renewable energy investment, energy storage, power sector modernization, and regional energy integration supporting energy security and climate commitments.$$,
