      $$Tunisia's agricultural sector produces olive oil (major exporter), dates, citrus fruits, cereals, vegetables, and livestock. Mediterranean climate supports diverse cultivation. Agro-processing and food industries contribute to manufacturing sector. Export markets include olive oil, dates, and seafood. Water scarcity and climate variability affect productivity. Government programs support agricultural modernization, irrigation, and organic farming. The sector represents opportunity for agro-processing investment, organic agriculture, value-added products, and agricultural value chains serving European export markets and domestic food processing industries.$$,
