      $$Tunisia produces phosphates for export and fertilizer production, alongside oil and gas. The country's mining sector contributes to export revenues and industrial supply chains. Phosphate sector faces infrastructure and investment challenges. Geological potential exists for additional mineral exploration. Mining sector modernization and private investment aim to expand production and efficiency. Environmental and social considerations influence development frameworks. The sector represents opportunity for phosphate sector revitalization, responsible mining investment, and mineral exploration supporting export revenues and industrial development.$$,
