    ('TUN', 'logistics_trade', 'Logistics and Trade',
      $$Tunisia's logistics infrastructure includes Mediterranean ports, road networks, European trade integration, free zones, and positioning as North African logistics hub.$$,
      $$Tunisia operates Mediterranean port facilities at Tunis-La Goulette, Radès, Sfax, and others serving imports, exports including manufacturing and agricultural products, and regional trade. Road networks connect regions and border crossings with Algeria and Libya. European Union Association Agreement supports preferential trade access. Free zones and industrial parks serve export manufacturing. Proximity to Europe positions Tunisia for logistics and distribution services. The sector represents opportunity for port modernization, logistics services, supply chain infrastructure, and Mediterranean trade hub development leveraging European proximity and manufacturing exports.$$,
