      $$Benin's financial sector combines banking infrastructure, substantial mobile money adoption, and expanding digital payment systems. West African Economic and Monetary Union (WAEMU) membership provides monetary stability and regional financial integration. Mobile money supports remittances, payments, and financial inclusion. Banking sector serves urban centers with microfinance reaching rural areas. Regional payment systems support cross-border transactions. The sector is positioned for digital banking expansion, mobile financial services growth, payment infrastructure investment, and financial inclusion initiatives serving formal and informal economy participants across Benin's diverse economic landscape.$$,
