      $$Benin's energy sector combines imported power, domestic generation expansion, solar deployment, and West African power pool participation addressing access and reliability.$$,
      $$Benin imports substantial electricity from neighboring countries while developing domestic generation capacity including solar and gas-fired plants. The country participates in West African Power Pool for regional electricity trade. Solar energy deployment is expanding for grid and off-grid applications. Energy access rates are improving but remain below full coverage. Government energy sector reforms aim to attract investment and expand generation. The sector represents opportunity for solar energy investment, domestic generation capacity, mini-grid deployment, and regional power integration supporting industrialization, electrification, and economic growth in a regional energy market context.$$,
