    ('BEN', 'agriculture_agribusiness', 'Agriculture and Agribusiness',
      $$Benin's agriculture includes cotton, cashews, pineapples, palm oil, and food crops supporting export revenues, rural livelihoods, and agro-processing potential.$$,
      $$Benin's agricultural sector produces cotton (major export), cashews, pineapples, palm oil, and food crops including cassava and maize. Agriculture supports majority of livelihoods and contributes substantially to GDP and exports. Government programs support agricultural modernization, value chain development, and agro-processing. Irrigation investment and climate-resilient farming represent priorities. Port of Cotonou facilitates agricultural exports and regional transit trade. The sector represents substantial opportunity for agro-processing investment, organic agriculture, value-added products, and agricultural finance serving export markets and food security in an agriculture-dependent economy with strong regional trade positioning.$$,
