      $$Benin's mining sector is at early development stages, with exploration for gold, iron ore, phosphates, limestone, and industrial minerals. Small-scale and artisanal gold mining exists. Government mining sector reforms aim to attract investment while establishing governance frameworks. Geological surveys support resource assessment. Mining sector development could diversify export revenues beyond cotton and agricultural products. The sector represents opportunity for responsible mining investment, mineral exploration, artisanal sector formalization, and resource governance supporting economic diversification and revenue generation as exploration advances and investment frameworks strengthen.$$,
      45, 68, 5, 'explorer'),
    ('BEN', 'logistics_trade', 'Logistics and Trade',
      $$Benin's logistics infrastructure is anchored by Cotonou Port serving landlocked neighbors, road corridors, ECOWAS integration, and positioning as West African gateway.$$,
      $$Benin's Port of Cotonou is a major West African port serving imports, exports, and substantial transit trade for landlocked Niger and northern Nigeria. Road corridors connect the port to hinterland markets. The country benefits from Economic Community of West African States (ECOWAS) integration and African Continental Free Trade Area participation. Free zones support trade and light manufacturing. Government port modernization and corridor efficiency programs target competitiveness. The sector represents substantial opportunity for port expansion, logistics services, corridor infrastructure, border trade facilitation, and regional distribution hub development leveraging Benin's coastal access and landlocked neighbor transit positioning.$$,
