      $$Benin offers tourism assets including UNESCO World Heritage sites with Royal Palaces of Abomey, Slave Route heritage at Ouidah, voodoo cultural tourism, coastal beaches, and Pendjari National Park wildlife. The country positions as a cultural and heritage tourism destination. Hospitality infrastructure exists in Cotonou and emerging tourist zones. Regional tourism and diaspora travel provide baseline visitors. Government tourism sector initiatives support destination development and marketing. The sector represents opportunity for heritage tourism investment, eco-tourism, cultural tourism development, and hospitality infrastructure serving West African regional tourism and niche international cultural heritage markets.$$,
