      $$Burkina Faso's financial sector is characterized by substantial mobile money adoption serving payments, remittances, and financial inclusion given limited traditional banking reach. West African Economic and Monetary Union membership provides monetary stability. Banking infrastructure serves urban centers with microfinance institutions reaching rural areas. Remittances from Burkinabè diaspora support household incomes. Mobile banking and agent networks expand financial access. The sector is positioned for mobile financial services expansion, digital payment infrastructure, microfinance growth, and financial inclusion initiatives serving predominantly informal economy, agricultural population, and youth demographic with strong mobile money foundation.$$,
