      $$Burkina Faso faces significant energy access challenges with low electrification rates, particularly in rural areas. The country imports electricity while developing domestic solar energy generation and mini-grids. Solar potential is substantial given Sahel climate. Biomass remains primary energy source for many households. Government electrification programs target access expansion through grid extension and off-grid solutions. Private sector investment in solar and mini-grids is growing. The sector represents significant opportunity for solar energy development, mini-grid deployment, energy access programs, and renewable energy investment supporting economic development, poverty reduction, and agricultural productivity in an energy-poor landlocked country.$$,
